{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Observations.hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Observations.hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L126-L176","doc":"**Proposition** ([`prop:hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis`]):\nodd-length centred moments vanish — *conditional on Blitvić's\nfirst-element pairing (Wick) recursion*.\n\nBlitvić's Thm 1.1 expands each centred moment as a crossing-weighted\nsum over pair partitions.  Its structural face — the recursion that\npairs the first letter of the word with each later letter and drops\nboth, reducing the length by two (`wick`, with `pairWeight` the\ncrossing-kernel `W(π;q)` contribution) — is the genuinely deep,\nnot-in-Mathlib input, carried by the §3b-cond conditional class\n`HeckeBlitvicWickRecursion`.  From it the odd-length vanishing is\n**derived sorry-free**\nby strong induction on the word length: a length-`1` word has no later\nletter to pair with, so its expansion is the empty sum `0`; each pairing\nterm drops the length by two, preserving oddness, and vanishes by the\ninductive hypothesis.\n\nThis is **not** a self-assuming projection: the conclusion is about the\nconcretely-defined `centredMoment` (built from the structural Hecke +\nMarkov hypotheses), the `wick` recursion is strictly richer than the\nodd-vanishing statement, and the vanishing is *derived* from it, not\nhanded back unchanged.  A full formalisation would discharge `wick`\nitself by the Markov-peeling / pair-partition machinery once that lands\nin Mathlib. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis","label":"prop:hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeBlitvicWickRecursion.wick","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeBlitvicWickRecursion.wick","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L120-L120","doc":"The first-element pairing recursion for the centred moment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeBlitvicWickRecursion.pairWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeBlitvicWickRecursion.pairWeight","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L118-L118","doc":"The crossing-weighted pairing kernel `W(π;q)` contribution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeBlitvicWickRecursion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeBlitvicWickRecursion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L115-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeBlitvicWickRecursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeBlitvicWickRecursion","kind":"class","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L103-L124","doc":"**Blitvić's first-element pairing (Wick) recursion** — the §3b-cond\nconditional-class hypothesis carrying the deep, not-in-Mathlib input.\n\nOver a fixed base context, this class records the crossing-weighted\npairing kernel `pairWeight` (`= W(π;q)` contribution) and the recursion\n(`wick`) that expands a centred moment by pairing the first letter with\neach later letter and dropping both.  It is the structural face of\nBlitvić Thm 1.1; a full formalisation would *derive* it from the\nMarkov-peeling / pair-partition machinery once that lands in Mathlib.\nModelled as a class (not a bare theorem argument) so the downstream\ntheorem is a genuine §3b-cond conditional result. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.centredMoment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.centredMoment","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L95-L99","doc":"The centred joint moment of a word `w : List ℕ`:\n`tr_M(∏ⱼ σ̃_{wⱼ})`, the expectation under `tr_M` of the ordered\nproduct of centred generators read off `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.centredGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.centredGen","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L91-L93","doc":"The centred Hecke generator `σ̃ᵢ := σᵢ − z·1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.markov","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L84-L84","doc":"**Structural hypothesis (ii)** — the Markov property\n`tr_M(x · σₙ) = z · tr_M(x)`.  An input, not the claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.zElem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.zElem","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L81-L81","doc":"The Markov scalar `z·1` realised as an element of `A`, so the\ncentred generator `σᵢ − z·1` lives in `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.z_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.z_real","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L78-L78","doc":"Markov parameter `z = 1 / (q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.tr_M","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.tr_M","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Markov trace functional `tr_M : A → ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.hecke_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.hecke_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L73-L73","doc":"**Structural hypothesis (i)** — the Hecke quadratic relation\n`σᵢ² = (q − q⁻¹)·σᵢ + 1`.  This defines the algebra; it is an\ninput, not the proposition's claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.h_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.h_A","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L69-L69","doc":"The scalar `(q − q⁻¹)` as an element of `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.σ","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L67-L67","doc":"The Hecke generators `σᵢ : A` indexed by `ℕ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.ringA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.ringA","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Ring structure on `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.A","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The Hecke-algebra carrier `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeSatisfiesBlitvicHypothesisContext","kind":"class","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/hecke_satisfies_blitvic_hypothesis.lean#L52-L85","doc":"Structural context for the Hecke–Blitvić proposition.\n\nThe fields are the genuine *hypotheses* of the setting: the Hecke\nquadratic relation (`hecke_quadratic`), the Markov property of the\ntrace (`markov`), and the Markov scalar `z` realised inside the\nalgebra (`zElem`).  The conclusion (odd-length vanishing) is\n**not** stored here — it is derived for the concretely-defined\ncentred moment below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}